+# Live Broadcom research consulted
+
+Research performed on 2026-08-14. The Product Interoperability Matrix is a
+client-rendered application, so I used it for the interoperability and upgrade
+path checks and used the linked Broadcom knowledge articles to record the
+actionable path and sequencing details below. The pinned snapshot remains the
+artifact authority where the live pages have moved on.
+
+## Matrix and method
+
+- https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability
+  - Consulted for product-pair interoperability across vCenter, ESX, vSAN,
+    NSX, VMware Live Site Recovery, vSphere Replication, VMware Live Recovery,
+    and VCF Protection and Recovery.
+- https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade
+  - Consulted for the source-to-target upgrade-path views for those products.
+- https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/343230/using-the-vmware-product-interoperabilit.html
+  - Confirmed the Broadcom procedure: use Interoperability for product pairs,
+    use Upgrade Path for source transitions, and expose patch/legacy releases
+    when a precise source is not shown by default.
+
+## Decisions by inventoried product
+
+- vCenter `vc-edge-01`: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  and https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326316/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vcenter-s.html
+  - Informed the VCF Installer convert/import path for a standalone vSphere 8
+    estate with NSX 4.x, the vCenter-before-host sequence, and the pinned 9.1 GA
+    target build `25370922`.
+- ESX hosts `esx-edge-01`, `esx-edge-02`, `esx-edge-03`, and
+  `esx-edge-04`: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?articleNumber=316595
+  - Confirmed source build `24859861` as ESXi 8.0 Update 3g and target build
+    `25370933` as ESX 9.1.0.0. The four hosts share that exact transition and
+    are handled as a rolling workload-domain host stage.
+- vSAN `vsan-edge-01`: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/327034/understanding-vsan-ondisk-format-version.html
+  and https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?articleNumber=316595
+  - Informed the coupling of the vSAN release to ESX, health/resync gating, and
+    upgrading all hosts before moving the cluster to the 9.1 on-disk format.
+- NSX `nsx-edge-01`: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425164/vcenter-upgrade-precheck-from-version-8x.html
+  and https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317797/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-nsx.html
+  - Confirmed that NSX 4.2.2.1 with vCenter 9.x is an upgrade-only combination:
+    import the deployment as a VCF workload domain, then use VCF-managed
+    lifecycle. Also confirmed NSX 9.1 build `25318225`.
+- Live Site Recovery `lsr-edge-01` and vSphere Replication `vr-edge-01`:
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/408127/steps-to-converge-to-vmware-live-recover.html
+  and https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html
+  - Confirmed both legacy appliances must be 9.0.2.2 or later before a fresh
+    VMware Live Recovery 9.0.4 deployment and convergence/configuration
+    migration, on both paired sites. The second article informed the final
+    unified VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1 target and build `25367487`.
+
+## Live-versus-pinned conflicts
+
+- The live vCenter build table now lists 9.1.0.0100 build `25417926` after the
+  9.1 GA build. The snapshot intentionally pins 9.1.0.0 build `25370922`.
+- The live ESX build table now lists 9.1.0.0100 build `25433460` after the 9.1
+  GA build and newer 8.0 U3 patches after U3g. The snapshot intentionally pins
+  target build `25370933` and the fixture's exact U3g build `24859861`.
+- The live NSX build table contains releases newer than the fixture's 4.2.2.1
+  source. This does not change the exact fixture transition or pinned 9.1
+  target build.
+- Article 444864 illustrates base 9.0.2 source builds `24639340` and
+  `24628338`, while this fixture pins later 9.0.2.2 builds `24639343` and
+  `24628359`. Article 408127 explicitly accepts 9.0.2.2 or later, so the
+  fixture uses the convergence path and retains its exact pinned builds.
